  "answer": "The **Enterprise segment** offers the strongest growth quality. Enterprise customers post the highest satisfaction (NPS 52 once fully onboarded [NL-011#NL-011-S08]) and the lowest monthly churn (1.3% [NL-012#NL-012-S03]; also confirmed in [NL-016#NL-016-S03]). They generated the most expansion revenue: $91,000 in Q2, representing 52.6% of all expansion revenue [NL-012#NL-012-S03], driven by multi-department scaling and custom SSO/compliance add-ons [NL-012#NL-012-S05]. Enterprise LTV:CAC is 16.0x versus 8.3x for SMB [NL-016#NL-016-S03], and combined mid-market + enterprise accounts generate 83.8% of recurring revenue [NL-016#NL-016-S03].\n\nIt still requires more implementation capacity because onboarding is the longest and most complex: an average of 8.7 weeks, reflecting permission-mapping challenges and security reviews [NL-012#NL-012-S03]. Customer onboarding remains a resource constraint, and automated tools are needed to streamline permission mapping and initial document cleanup [NL-012#NL-012-S09]. Enterprise clients are vulnerable to implementation-phase delays [NL-011#NL-011-S08], and sales must navigate their security reviews, which makes the enterprise sales cycle more painful [NL-015#NL-015-S03].\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
